module Main
import Base
import Control

-- CHARACTERIZATION of the resume-site obligation (slice 4b-dprime).
--
-- `replay` RECEIVES an already-suspended coroutine with an arbitrary residual
-- row e and resumes it with `run`. One might expect this to be REJECTED unless
-- `replay` handles e (it performs the parked tail's effects). It is NOT: a
-- polymorphic residual contributes no concrete obligation, so `replay` type-
-- checks as effect-polymorphic and the residual is ABSORBED into its scheme.
--
-- This is sound -- `start` eagerly demands the full residual at the lifecycle
-- root, and second-class carriers keep every resume dynamically inside that
-- scope, so the handler is always present. But it means a generic resume driver
-- hides the tail's effects from its own signature. If we later make control
-- explicit (force resume drivers to declare `with eff e`), this golden flips
-- from an effect-polymorphic scheme to one carrying the residual -- a conscious
-- gate on that decision.
replay : Suspension U64 U64 U64 (row e) -> U64 with eff e
replay g = run g 0

main : U64
main = 0
